CSF compatibility changes for tools_opam 1.0.0.beta.1
===================================================

This is a unified diff against the pinned upstream release, not a standalone
program. Bazel's single_version_override applies it after downloading that
release, with patch_strip = 1. A leading + adds source, - removes source, and
a space-prefixed context line locates the edit. The /dev/null section adds the
small Python helper to the dependency; it is not a second CSF entry point.

Upstream: https://github.com/obazl/tools_opam/releases/tag/1.0.0.beta.1
Maintenance notes, preparation stages and verification: README.md beside this
patch. Both standalone and monorepo builds apply this same compiler-owned file.

Sections, in upstream path order:
  extensions/BUILD.bazel             Export the configure timestamp helper.
  extensions/opam.bzl                Bazel 9 invocation and locked stage graph.
  extensions/opam/opam_dep.bzl       Make imports depend on completed preparation.
  extensions/opam/opam_ops.bzl       Use Bazel's file-existence primitive.
  extensions/opam/opam_toolchain_xdg.bzl
                                    Split bootstrap from native installation.
  extensions/preserve_configure_mtime.py
                                    Run configure; reuse only identical inputs.

The five-minute jobs split work, not validation: the final package graph must
match the lock, and the real upstream compiler build/install still executes.

